## 6️⃣ State Management (Redux Toolkit)

```ts
// src/store/cartSlice.ts
import { createSlice, PayloadAction } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';

interface CartItem {
  productId: string;
  quantity: number;
}

interface CartState {
  items: CartItem[];
}

const initialState: CartState = { items: [] };

export const cartSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'cart',
  initialState,
  reducers: {
    addToCart(state, action: PayloadAction<CartItem>) {
      const existing = state.items.find(i => i.productId === action.payload.productId);
      if (existing) {
        existing.quantity += action.payload.quantity;
      } else {
        state.items.push(action.payload);
      }
    },
    removeFromCart(state, action: PayloadAction<string>) {
      state.items = state.items.filter(i => i.productId !== action.payload);
    },
    clearCart(state) {
      state.items = [];
    },
  },
});

export const { addToCart, removeFromCart, clearCart } = cartSlice.actions;
export default cartSlice.reducer;
```

---

## 7️⃣ API Client (Axios + Interceptors)

```ts
// src/lib/api.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL,
  timeout: 10000,
});

api.interceptors.request.use(config => {
  const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
  if (token) config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
  return config;
});

export default api;
```

---

## 8️⃣ Authentication Flow

1. **Login Page** – POST `/auth/login` → store JWT in `localStorage`.  
2. **Protected Routes** – Wrap with `withAuth` HOC that checks token expiry.  
3. **Refresh Token** – Call `/auth/refresh` before token expires.  

```tsx
// src/hooks/useAuth.ts
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import api from '../lib/api';

export const useAuth = () => {
  const [user, setUser] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    const token = localStorage.getItem('token');
    if (!token) return;
    api.get('/me').then(res => setUser(res.data));
  }, []);

  return { user };
};
```

---

## 9️⃣ Routing & Data Fetching (Next.js)

```tsx
// src/pages/index.tsx
import { GetStaticProps } from 'next';
import api from '../lib/api';
import { ProductCard } from '../components/ProductCard';

export const getStaticProps: GetStaticProps = async () => {
  const res = await api.get('/products?limit=20');
  return { props: { products: res.data } };
};

export default function Home({ products }) {
  return (
    <main className="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-6 p-4">
      {products.map(p => (
        <ProductCard key={p.id} {...p} />
      ))}
    </main>
  );
}
```

> **Why `getStaticProps`?**  
> • Generates static pages at build time → instant load.  
> • Revalidate with `revalidate: 60` for incremental static regeneration.

---

## 🔟 Checkout Flow

1. **Cart Page** – List items, allow quantity changes.  
2. **Checkout Page** – Collect shipping address, payment method.  
3. **Payment Integration** – Stripe Elements or PayPal SDK.  
4. **Order Confirmation** – Show order summary, send email via backend webhook.

```tsx
// src/pages/checkout.tsx
import { useForm } from 'react-hook-form';
import api from '../lib/api';

export default function Checkout() {
  const { register, handleSubmit } = useForm();

  const onSubmit = async data => {
    const res = await api.post('/orders', data);
    // redirect to confirmation
  };

  return (
    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className="max-w-xl mx-auto p-4">
      <input {...register('name')} placeholder="Full Name" required />
      <input {...register('address')} placeholder="Address" required />
      {/* Payment fields */}
      <button type="submit" className="btn-primary mt-4">Place Order</button>
    </form>
  );
}
```

---

## 1️⃣1️⃣ Performance Optimizations

| Technique | How |
|-----------|-----|
| **Image Optimization** | Use Next.js `<Image>` component; serve WebP. |
| **Code Splitting** | Dynamic imports (`next/dynamic`). |
| **Lazy Load Offscreen Content** | IntersectionObserver or `loading="lazy"`. |
| **Prefetch Links** | `next/link` automatically prefetches. |
| **Bundle Analysis** | `next-bundle-analyzer` plugin. |
| **Cache Headers** | CDN (Cloudflare, Vercel Edge) with long TTL. |

---

## 1️⃣2️⃣ Accessibility & SEO

| ✅ | Item |
|---|------|
| Semantic HTML | `<header>`, `<nav>`, `<main>`, `<footer>` |
| Alt Text | All images have meaningful `alt`. |
| Keyboard Navigation | Focus rings, `tabindex`. |
| ARIA Roles | `role="navigation"`, `aria-label`. |
| Meta Tags | `<meta name="description">`, `<meta property="og:image">`. |
| Structured Data | JSON‑LD for products (`schema.org/Product`). |

---

## 1️⃣3️⃣ Testing Strategy

| Layer | Tool | Example |
|-------|------|---------|
| Unit | Jest + React Testing Library | Test component renders correctly. |
| Integration | Cypress | Simulate adding to cart → checkout. |
| Visual | Percy | Snapshot regression. |

```tsx
// src/components/__tests__/ProductCard.test.tsx
import { render } from '@testing-library/react';
import { ProductCard } from '../ProductCard';

test('renders product card', () => {
  const { getByText } = render(
    <ProductCard id="1" title="Test" price={9.99} imageUrl="/img.png" />
  );
  expect(getByText('Test')).toBeInTheDocument();
});
```

---

## 1️⃣4️⃣ Deployment Pipeline

| Stage | Tool | Notes |
|-------|------|-------|
| CI | GitHub Actions | Run tests, lint, build. |
| Build | Vercel | Deploy on push to `main`. |
| CDN | Vercel Edge | Automatic caching. |
| Monitoring | Sentry | Capture runtime errors. |
| Analytics | Plausible / Google Analytics | Track conversions. |

```yaml
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml
name: Deploy
on:
  push:
    branches: [main]
jobs:
  build:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3
        with:
          node-version: '20'
      - run: npm ci
      - run: npm run lint
      - run: npm test
      - run: npm run build
      - uses: amondnet/vercel-action@v20
        with:
          vercel-token: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_TOKEN }}
          vercel-org-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_ORG_ID }}
          vercel-project-id: ${{ secrets.VERCEL_PROJECT_ID }}
```

---

## 1️⃣5️⃣ Security Checklist

| ✅ | Item |
|---|------|
| CSRF Protection | Use SameSite cookies or CSRF tokens. |
| XSS Prevention | Escape user input, use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` sparingly. |
| HTTPS | Enforce TLS everywhere. |
| Rate Limiting | Backend side (e.g., Cloudflare Workers). |
| CORS Policy | Restrict origins to your domain. |
| Secrets Management | Store API keys in `.env` and never commit. |

---

## 1️⃣6️⃣ Documentation & Handoff

| Tool | Use |
|------|-----|
| **Storybook** | Document UI components. |
| **Docz / Docusaurus** | API docs, developer guide. |
| **Confluence / Notion** | Project specs, design decisions. |

---

## 1️⃣7️⃣ Quick Checklist Before Launch

- [ ] All pages are responsive (mobile → desktop).  
- [ ] Lighthouse score ≥ 90 (performance, accessibility, best practices).  
- [ ] All forms validated client‑side + server‑side.  
- [ ] Payment gateway sandbox tested.  
- [ ] SEO meta tags & structured data added.  
- [ ] Error boundaries in place.  
- [ ] Analytics & error monitoring configured.  
- [ ] CI pipeline passes all tests.  
- [ ] Production build size < 200 KB.  

---

## 🎉 Final Thoughts

Building a robust e‑commerce frontend is a marathon, not a sprint.  
Start small (MVP), iterate based on real user feedback, and keep the codebase clean with solid tooling.  
If you hit roadblocks—whether it’s state management, API integration, or performance tuning—feel free to ask for more targeted help. Happy coding!
